{"base_rate":0.4226475279106858,"brier":0.4369535885167465,"bss":-0.790671607422079,"bss_hi":-0.5978421257023019,"bss_lo":-1.047468080134339,"chart":{"base":[610.0,124.1],"lead":"62,250.6 272,234.7 482,229.7 692,228.1","note":{"base":"skill -0.79 — higher than 1% of cities","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 48% of cities","rel":"promised 63% → rained 14%; promised 100% → rained 64%"},"rel":"458.6,406.8 613.9,360.6 670.5,283.9 691.5,187.5"},"country":"CO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.4728708133971292,"ess":335.5783221976168,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Cali</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Cali rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>64%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(51%), there is still roughly a <b>10%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 627 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 19.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.79, ranked 210 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(208&ndash;211) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>76%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>54</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>52%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>259</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Cali</b> <span class=\"muted\">Colombia</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.79</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>208&ndash;211\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>627 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Cali &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Cali\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"237.58476190476193,156.66666666666666 325.5891803278688,71.7049180327869 355.81888888888886,44.96296296296293 377.78000000000003,28.550724637681185 395.71600000000007,18.0 404.04950819672126,18.0 411.71297297297303,18.0 411.71297297297303,19.405405405405418 404.04950819672126,41.86885245901635 395.71600000000007,54.39999999999998 377.78000000000003,81.30434782608694 355.81888888888886,112.37037037037038 325.5891803278688,143.31147540983608 237.58476190476193,237.55555555555557\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"228.15629984051037\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"228.15629984051037\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"237.58476190476193,347.3333333333333 325.5891803278688,316.3606557377049 355.81888888888886,294.3703703703704 377.78000000000003,292.3188405797101 395.71600000000007,266.73333333333335 404.04950819672126,191.04918032786884 411.71297297297303,147.2972972972973\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 51%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"237.58476190476193\" cy=\"347.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 76%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"325.5891803278688\" cy=\"316.3606557377049\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 54 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"355.81888888888886\" cy=\"294.3703703703704\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"377.78000000000003\" cy=\"292.3188405797101\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 95%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 60 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"395.71600000000007\" cy=\"266.73333333333335\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 52% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"404.04950819672126\" cy=\"191.04918032786884\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 259 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.71297297297303\" cy=\"147.2972972972973\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(42%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Cali the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (-0.51) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-1.28).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>-1.277</td><td class='num'>54.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>150</td><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'>-0.846</td><td class='num'>48.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>147</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>-0.755</td><td class='num'>47.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>153</td><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'>-0.508</td><td class='num'>38.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":3.43054,"lon":-76.5199,"n":627,"n_cities":213,"name":"Cali","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.676,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.5073015873015874,"n":63,"obs":0.09523809523809523,"sig":true},{"hi":0.82,"lo":0.676,"mean":0.7559016393442621,"n":61,"obs":0.18032786885245902,"sig":true},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.82,"mean":0.8412962962962962,"n":54,"obs":0.24074074074074073,"sig":true},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9033333333333334,"n":69,"obs":0.2463768115942029,"sig":true},{"hi":0.97,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9540000000000002,"n":60,"obs":0.31666666666666665,"sig":true},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.97,"mean":0.9775409836065572,"n":61,"obs":0.5245901639344263,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9991891891891893,"n":259,"obs":0.6447876447876448,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":19.8,"provisional":false,"rank":210,"rank_hi":211.0,"rank_lo":207.975,"reliability":0.23856235200616005,"resolution":0.04522259051245607,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"cali","station":"","timezone":"America/Bogota"}